# Logs
logs
*.log
# ...but run logs are evidence of what was executed on chain, and belong in
# history. Before this, *.log plus 20 one-off `git add -f` calls meant 12 logs
# were silently absent - the split even cut through a single campaign
# (merge-zcash-nu7-v3-run.log ignored while its -v2- and -v3-round2- siblings
# were tracked). Un-ignore by directory instead.
!archive/runs/**/*.log
!runs/**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
.env

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Local Netlify folder
.netlify

#codegen
src/gql

# refactor-diff writes the OLD version of a script here to execute it, and
# removes it again. A killed run can leave one behind; it is never wanted.
_refactor_diff_old_*

# A dry run's transcript is a preview, not evidence — it is regenerated every
# time and would otherwise pile up. Live transcripts and progress logs stay.
runs/**/dry-*.log

# Scratch scripts used while reorganising. Never wanted in a commit; one
# _refactor_diff_old_ copy already slipped in once.
_tmp_*

# tools/schedule.js runtime state: the tick log, the lock, and the Windows task
# definition `install` generates. Machine-local; the record of a scheduled run
# is its entry in lifecycle/<slug>.json plus runs/<slug>/scheduled/*.log.
runs/scheduler.log
runs/scheduler.lock
runs/scheduler-task.xml
